00:11:28,888 --> 00:11:34,888
Mark William Calaway (born March 24, 1965), better known by his ring name
the Undertaker, is an American retired professional wrestler.

11
00:12:37,777 --> 00:12:43,777
He is signed to WWE, where he is a brand ambassador and a writer for
its sister promotion Lucha Libre AAA Worldwide (AAA).

12
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:52,666
Widely regarded as one of the greatest professional wrestlers of all time, Calaway spent the vast
majority of his career wrestling for WWE and in 2022 was inducted into the WWE Hall of Fame.

13
00:14:55,555 --> 00:15:01,555
Calaway began his career in 1987, working under various gimmicks for World Class
Championship Wrestling (WCCW) and other affiliate promotions.

14
00:16:04,444 --> 00:16:10,444
He signed with World Championship Wrestling (WCW) in 1989 for a brief stint, and
then joined the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE) in 1990.

15
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:19,333
Calaway rebranded himself as "The Undertaker" when he joined the WWF.

16
00:18:22,222 --> 00:18:28,222
As one of WWE's most high-profile and enduring characters, The Undertaker is famed for his funerary themeing around an undead, macabre "Deadman" persona, which
gained significant mainstream popularity and won him the Wrestling Observer Newsletter award for Best Gimmick a record-setting 5 years in a row.

17
00:19:31,111 --> 00:19:37,111
He is the longest-tenured wrestler in company history at 30 years.

18
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:46,000
In 2000, the Undertaker adopted a biker identity nicknamed "American Badass".

19
00:21:48,888 --> 00:21:54,888
Calaway resurrected the Deadman gimmick in 2004, with residual
elements of the "American Badass" remaining.

20
00:22:57,777 --> 00:23:03,777
The Undertaker was known for his role in WWE's flagship event WrestleMania.

21
00:24:06,666 --> 00:24:12,666
He achieved 21 consecutive victories at
WrestleMania, referred to in WWE as The Streak.

22
00:25:15,555 --> 00:25:21,555
He headlined the event five times (13, 24, 26, 33, and 36 – Night 1).

23
00:26:24,444 --> 00:26:30,444
He is also known for pairing with his in-storyline half-brother Kane, with whom he
alternatively feuded and teamed (as the Brothers of Destruction) from 1997 through 2020.

24
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:39,333
During his wrestling career under the Undertaker gimmick, Calaway won the WWF/E Championship four times, the World
Heavyweight Championship three times, the Hardcore Championship once and the World Tag Team Championship six times.

25
00:28:42,222 --> 00:28:48,222
He also won the Royal Rumble match in 2007.

26
00:29:51,111 --> 00:29:57,111
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
